          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em Stone–Weierstrass theorem
            says given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+space"} compact Hausdorff space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to \mathbb{R}
            by elements of any subalgebra that has enough elements to distinguish points. It is a far-reaching generalization of a classical theorem of Weierstrass, that real-valued continuous functions on a closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval"} interval
            are uniformly approximable by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial"} polynomial
            functions.
          %h2#precise_statement Precise statement
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+space"} compact Hausdorff topological space
          %p
            (For a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive
            version take
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to be a compact regular
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locale"} locale
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+space"} compact Hausdorff space
          %p
            Recall that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+functions"} algebra of
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \to \mathbb{R}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative
            (real)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Banach+algebra"} Banach algebra
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit"} unit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm"} norm
            is the sup-norm
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi sup
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\| f\| \;\coloneqq\; sup_{x \in X} {|f(x)|}
                  \\,.
          %p
            A
            %strong subalgebra
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(X)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+subspace"} vector subspace
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \subseteq C(X)
            that is closed under the unit and algebra multiplication operations on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
